                    cm_insights:            `What decided it`,
                    title:                  `Program Designer`,
                    subtitle:               `The Dean greenlit a new applied-data-and-AI program for non-technical managers — but set hard guardrails: a $180,000 development-cost cap, a break-even of 60 paid enrollments across two cohorts, and a launch at the 75-day gate. Design who it is for, how it is delivered, and what it costs the learner. The most ambitious design rarely breaks even fastest; the cheapest to build is rarely the one learners pay for or finish.`,
